            <p class="lt-chem-151409">\(\eta\)<sup>n</sup> where n is the number of attached atoms; used when the coordinated atoms are all connected by bonds. Usually the metal-ligand bonding involves \(\pi\)-type coordination.</p>

            <p class="lt-chem-151409">In speech, \(\eta^1\)=monohapto; \(\eta^2\)=dihapto; \(\eta^3\)=trihapto, etc.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
